{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    This sequence is defined with four base cases and a four-term recurrence relation.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the last four values for n=0, 1, 2, 3 respectively\n    f_n_minus_4 = 0  # fib4(0)\n    f_n_minus_3 = 0  # fib4(1)\n    f_n_minus_2 = 2  # fib4(2)\n    f_n_minus_1 = 0  # fib4(3)\n\n    # Calculate fib4(n) for n >= 4\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        current_fib = f_n_minus_1 + f_n_minus_2 + f_n_minus_3 + f_n_minus_4\n        f_n_minus_4 = f_n_minus_3\n        f_n_minus_3 = f_n_minus_2\n        f_n_minus_2 = f_n_minus_1\n        f_n_minus_1 = current_fib\n\n    return f_n_minus_1"}
