{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "def monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a list is monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    Allows equal adjacent values (non-decreasing or non-increasing).\"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    non_decreasing = True\n    non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(len(l) - 1):\n        if l[i] < l[i+1]:\n            non_increasing = False\n        if l[i] > l[i+1]:\n            non_decreasing = False\n\n        if not non_decreasing and not non_increasing:\n            return False\n\n    return non_decreasing or non_increasing"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/58", "solution": "def common(l1: list, l2: list):\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique common elements for two lists, handling unhashable or uncomparable items.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Primary algorithm: convert to sets, find intersection, then convert to list.\n        s1 = set(l1)\n        s2 = set(l2)\n        common_elements = list(s1.intersection(s2))\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback for unhashable elements: nested loops collecting unique matches.\n        common_elements = []\n        for item1 in l1:\n            if any(item1 == seen for seen in common_elements):\n                continue\n            for item2 in l2:\n                if item1 == item2:\n                    common_elements.append(item1)\n                    break\n\n    try:\n        # Attempt to sort naturally.\n        common_elements.sort()\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback for non-comparable elements: sort by string representation for determinism.\n        common_elements.sort(key=repr)\n\n    return common_elements"}
