{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\"\"\"\n    max_prime_factor = 1\n\n    # Divide by 2 until n is odd.\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        max_prime_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Check for odd factors starting from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            max_prime_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor.\n    if n > 1:\n        max_prime_factor = n\n\n    return max_prime_factor"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the derivative of a polynomial represented by coefficients.\n    The polynomial is xs[0] + xs[1]*x + xs[2]*x^2 + ....\n    \"\"\"\n    # The derivative of c*x^n is c*n*x^(n-1).\n    # The new coefficient for x^i is (i+1) * original_xs[i+1].\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(xs) - 1):\n        result.append(xs[i+1] * (i+1))\n    return result"}
