{"task_id": "HumanEval/75", "solution": "def is_multiply_prime(a):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return True if integer a is the product of exactly three prime numbers\n    (primes may repeat), otherwise False.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, int):\n        return False\n    if a < 8:  # smallest product of three primes is 2*2*2 = 8\n        return False\n\n    n = a\n    count = 0\n    p = 2\n    while p * p <= n:\n        while n % p == 0:\n            count += 1\n            n //= p\n            if count > 3:\n                return False\n        p += 1 if p == 2 else 2  # check 2, then only odd divisors\n\n    if n > 1:\n        count += 1\n\n    return count == 3"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "def is_simple_power(x, n):\n    # Accept integer-like inputs only\n    if not isinstance(x, int):\n        if isinstance(x, float) and x.is_integer():\n            x = int(x)\n        else:\n            return False\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        if isinstance(n, float) and n.is_integer():\n            n = int(n)\n        else:\n            return False\n\n    # Handle special bases first\n    if n == 0:\n        # 0**k == 0 for any positive integer k; 0**0 is undefined -> treat (1,0) as False\n        return x == 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return x == 1\n    if n == -1:\n        return x in (1, -1)\n\n    # Handle trivial x values\n    if x == 0:\n        return False  # non-zero base cannot produce 0\n    if x == 1:\n        return True  # any base**0 == 1\n\n    # Repeatedly divide x by n while divisible\n    current = x\n    while current % n == 0:\n        current //= n\n\n    return current == 1"}
