{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input types\n    if not isinstance(a, int) or not isinstance(b, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"a and b must be integers\")\n    # Validate positivity as per specification\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"a and b must be positive integers\")\n\n    lo, hi = min(a, b), max(a, b)\n    # Find first even >= lo\n    start = lo if lo % 2 == 0 else lo + 1\n    if start > hi:\n        return []\n    # Generate evens efficiently\n    evens = list(range(start, hi + 1, 2))\n    # Filter to single-digit even digits (0-9) if the intent is \"digits\"\n    # The original examples imply treating values like 10-14 -> [] because\n    # there are no single-digit evens in that range, so enforce 0-9.\n    return [x for x in evens if 0 <= x <= 9]"}
